{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]],"date-time":"2026-09-09T10:08:26Z","timestamp":1788948506410,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":108,"publisher":"Wiley","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]],"date-time":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1788912000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]],"date-time":"2026-09-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1788912000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100013549","name":"Bundesministerium f\u00fcr Umwelt, Naturschutz, nukleare Sicherheit und Verbraucherschutz","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["67DAS145A"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["67DAS145A"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100013549","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100002347","name":"Bundesministerium f\u00fcr Bildung und Forschung","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["033L216A"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["033L216A"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100002347","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Bus Strat Env"],"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>This study explores how companies perceive risks stemming from climate change as a gradual process, focusing on the logistics sector. It advances research on organizational climate risk perception by integrating perspectives on embeddedness and resource configurations. Based on 41 semi\u2010structured interviews with representatives of 22 logistics companies in the Osnabr\u00fcck region, we find that firms' resource configurations shape their capacity to perceive climate risks: Resource\u2010rich firms are more adept due to human resource slack, allowing them to process and document climate\u2010related sensory experiences and undertake anticipatory exercises. In contrast, resource\u2010poor firms display unrealistic optimism, leading to inadequate preparedness. While territorial embeddedness can broaden experience with climate impacts, embeddedness in interorganizational networks provides limited support for climate risk perception. Overall, sensory experiences and internal resource allocation\u2014particularly human capital dedicated to future\u2010oriented thinking\u2014constitute antecedents of organizational climate risk perception, a critical prerequisite for adaptive capacity.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/bse.71470","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]],"date-time":"2026-09-09T09:30:07Z","timestamp":1788946207000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Why Some Firms Perceive Climate Risks and Others Do Not\u2014Evidence From the Logistics Sector"],"prefix":"10.1002","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7326-3774","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Felix","family":"B\u00fccken","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geography Osnabr\u00fcck University  Osnabr\u00fcck Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1187-5166","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Martin","family":"Franz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geography Osnabr\u00fcck University  Osnabr\u00fcck Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,9]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_12_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/bse.2552"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1108\/09534810010310258"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jclepro.2010.10.017"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_5_1","doi-as